@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-no-user-credentials
The legacy private connection talks to the one server set in Settings. Its credentials are
the optional Cloudflare Access client ID and secret (or an in-app Access sign-in's token,
settings-access-sign-in-in-app) and the account's session, which are
sent only to that server, stored only on the phone, and never logged or shown back in
full. The account's password is sent once, to sign in, and never stored (Tavi, 16 Oct
12:47). The session MUST go only to the server address it signed in on, and the password
and session MUST NOT go over plain HTTP except to this phone or the emulator's host
(Devin Review on PR 58).
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal GitHub decision adds a separate app-owned HTTPS account
origin. A personal Pully bearer MUST use only that origin's fixed personal routes or
the captured /workspace/api/rpc and /workspace/api/events routes (Tavi25Oct2026,
one GitHub login) and
MUST NOT become a legacy session, Access credential or GitHub REST credential. Android
MUST encrypt pending and accepted personal bearers with a non-exportable Keystore key
in storage excluded from backup; native errors MUST NOT expose its contents. GitHub
and provider credentials MUST remain on the server. This deliberately scopes the old
one-server-only credential rule to the compatibility connection.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] data-account-discovery-keeps-evidence
A fresh private-server installation MUST retain discovery failures as actionable
connection state instead of silently presenting an empty connected Inbox. A successful
Pully response MAY establish connectivity without inventing account capabilities for
an older server. HTML, non-RPC authentication failures, unavailable or malformed account
responses MUST NOT forget an existing session. A source change MUST retire discovered
capabilities and hide an identity belonging to a different server; stale checks MUST
NOT overwrite the current source or a newer check. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 reinstall
screenshot and request for clear account/connection guidance.
Unmarked legacy capabilities MUST be rediscovered rather than attributed to the current
server. A matching saved session MUST retain offline access during that discovery
(21 Oct 2026 first-run review, legacy server replacement regression).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-settings-sync
While signed in, the phone's choices of look, language, layout, fonts, code size, sounds,
vibration, AI effort and Analyze, which repositories the Inbox hides and the Inbox chip
last picked (P1), are kept on the
account, each with when it changed, and the newer change of each wins; a change made while
a sync is out is never undone by it, and choices made before the first sync count as the
oldest, so they reach an account without them but never override another phone's. The server and its
Access secrets, the session, Update notifications and Usage stats stay on the phone
("start saving settings, both on the mobile app and also sync it": Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] settings-sync-policy-keeps-native-owner-lazy
