Tours the person has opened are stored on the phone, so they open at once the next time
(CHANGELOG 0.28.0).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-jev-polls-briefly
While Inbox rows lack Jev's read and the Inbox needs it, the phone reads `my-pulls-cached`
with `revalidate: false` and `classify: true` every three seconds for two minutes at most,
and never shows a loading screen for it (architecture, Jev; rule 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-file-marks-follow-the-head
The phone drops a diff's file marks when the pull request's head moves, and shows Jev's
read only for the current head and title (architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] data-posts-selected-critique-revision
Posting findings MUST send the displayed critique's variant, immutable revision and
head SHA with its selected IDs. A newer displayed result MUST reset selection, and a
late post of an older result MUST NOT mark the new result posted (repository review
15 Oct 2026, finding 8).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-analytics-queue-on-disk
Every usage event the phone tracks MUST be written to `filesDir/analytics/queue.ndjson`
as well as kept in memory, so no network and a killed app lose nothing: a crash's own
event is written to that file on the crashing thread, and what is left goes up on the
next start or with a WorkManager job that waits for a network. The queue keeps at most
5,000 events, dropping the oldest, and sends them to `POST /api/events` on the server set
in Settings, with the same Access headers as `/api/rpc`, at most 200 a call. It MUST NOT
use any analytics, crash or telemetry package (message 15 Oct 20:58, "We will track them
directly on our server. No need for fancy packages", and 21:12, "doit"; plan "Pulls
analytics on our own server").
In the anonymous Explore entry mode, private analytics MUST be paused without changing
the saved Usage stats choice or discarding a returning account's queued events. Guest
startup and workers MUST NOT send events to an unverified/private server. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 ordinary signed-out browsing and isolated guest-authority decision.
Guest intervals MUST NOT later enter private screen/foreground durations, and a
private entry reached after guest startup MUST NOT be counted as a slow app launch
(22 Oct 2026 Compound guest review).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-analytics-counts-not-content
An event's props MUST carry only counts, timings, fixed choices, on or off values and a
pull request's repository and number. The phone MUST NOT send a file's name or path (a
file is its extension only), search or Ask text, a diff, code, a comment, an AI answer, a
title, a server address or any credential, and it drops every prop key the server would
drop (`AnalyticsRules.cleanProps`) before the event is queued. A screen is one of a fixed
set of lowercase words and a server call is its RPC name only, never its arguments. A
crash or a failed load carries only the error's class, its own message cut short, the top
frames of its stack and the screen (plan "Pulls analytics on our own server",
Guardrails; message 15 Oct 20:58).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] github-native-adapter-never-adopts-legacy-state
Repo(Context), Account display, model settings, Home caches, tours and synced settings
MUST use the mounted workspace's immutable accountId namespace in GitHub mode. They
MUST NOT read the saved legacy account session, server credentials or owner preferences
as that workspace's identity or data. Personal bearer custody MUST remain in the secure
personal vault/runtime; the adapter MUST NOT persist it. Native source retirement MUST
invalidate private services, callbacks and cached rows synchronously. Explicit custom
server setup MAY return to the preserved ExistingServer compatibility flow.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026, restore production native services with each GitHub account's
own data and no legacy credential or preference adoption.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] github-analytics-uses-its-own-shared-queue
GitHub workspace usage MUST use UsageAnalyticsQueue with an immutable-account namespace
under analytics-workspace, separate from the legacy analytics queue and metadata. Its
sanitized events MUST use only the captured /workspace/api/events transport; switching
accounts or losing native foreground authority MUST cancel uploads and retire the old
queue before another account appears. Old durable events MAY retry only after that
same account is freshly verified. Usage stats off MUST clear that account's queue and
cancel its uploads. No legacy events or guest intervals MAY be adopted.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026, full production Stats under the owned single-login workspace and
the settled authenticated workspace events route.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] active-account-settings-reach-root-consumers
The Activity's palette, light/dark choice, language, app/code fonts, sounds and haptics
MUST resolve the currently selected account's settings when native ownership changes.
GitHub consumers MUST NOT retain a legacy settings object captured before login.
Without a mounted workspace, Explore/GitHub local preferences MAY use only the accepted
private vault record's immutable-account namespace; that lookup MUST NOT verify a
profile or grant request authority. Missing/unavailable accepted storage MUST select
isolated Explore defaults. ExistingServer MUST select its preserved compatibility
preferences. This includes the update notification choice on cold worker startup.
Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 review-fix batch #1 and the parent's #1/#7 cold updater
preference integration observation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] native-workspace-pause-retains-presentation
A same-session foreground pause MUST retire the workspace transport and usage uploader
without invalidating the native repository epoch, account settings or private view
caches. Resume MUST bind new dispatch to fresh foreground admission for that same
captured session. Actual account/source retirement MUST still close private services,
invalidate their epoch and resynchronize existing update scheduling before replacement.
Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 coupled review-fix batch #1/#2 and updater coordination.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] github-workspace-admission-resumes-existing-observers
A GitHub workspace transport retirement MUST synchronously revoke registered native
read admission and clear the global AI-work follower/notice. After installing the
same session's fresh foreground transport, the binding MUST replay read admission and
reattach the real AiWork observer to already-running server tasks. ON_START or unchanged
account fields MUST NOT substitute for this post-admission restart. Observation MUST
NOT start or replay an AI task, revive a retired transport or replace presentation
identity. ExistingServer retains its separate lifecycle behavior. Source: Tavi's
25 Oct 2026 implementation followup to android-verification.json findings 1 and 2.
